    "q-330845": {
      "dom_id": "step-q330845",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "For the function\n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{720}{{s}^{8}},\\,s>0\n$$\n\nfind the inverse Laplace transform of $G(s),$ given that\n$L\\{{t}^{n}\\}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that we can write $G(s)$ as \n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{720}{{s}^{8}}=\\frac{F(s)}{s},\n$$\n\nwhere $F(s)=\\frac{720}{{s}^{7}}.$\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\nL\\{{t}^{n}\\}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.\n$$\n\nThus, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}\\{F(s)\\} & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{720}{{s}^{7}}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{6!}{{s}^{6+1}}\\} \\\\  & ={t}^{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we know that if $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ\\}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nUsing the property above in reverse, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}\\{G(s)\\} & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{F(s)}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}{τ}^{6}\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{7}}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-330845-a",
